1
00:00:57,819 --> 00:00:59,446
This is Media Break.

2
00:00:59,529 --> 00:01:02,999
You give us three minutes
and we'll give you the world.

3
00:01:03,200 --> 00:01:06,044
Good morning.
I'm Casey Wong with Jesse Perkins.

4
00:01:06,119 --> 00:01:07,917
Top story, Pretoria.

5
00:01:08,121 --> 00:01:09,919
The threat of nuclear confrontation

6
00:01:09,998 --> 00:01:12,046
in South Africa escalated today

7
00:01:12,125 --> 00:01:13,923
when the ruling
white military government

8
00:01:14,002 --> 00:01:18,052
of that besieged city-state
unveiled a French-made neutron bomb

9
00:01:18,131 --> 00:01:21,385
and affirmed its willingness
to use the three megaton device

10
00:01:21,468 --> 00:01:23,972
as the city's last line of defense.

11
00:01:24,639 --> 00:01:26,733
And the President's
first press conference

12
00:01:26,808 --> 00:01:29,311
from the Star Wars
orbiting peace platform

13
00:01:29,394 --> 00:01:31,067
got off to a shaky start,

14
00:01:31,145 --> 00:01:33,147
when power failed causing a brief,

15
00:01:33,231 --> 00:01:35,199
but harmless,
period of weightlessness

16
00:01:35,274 --> 00:01:37,868
for the visiting
President and his staff.

17
00:01:37,944 --> 00:01:39,992
We'll be back in a moment.

18
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:42,828
Is it time for that big operation?

19
00:01:42,907 --> 00:01:46,286
This may be the most
important decision of your life.

20
00:01:46,536 --> 00:01:50,291
So come down and talk to one
of our qualified surgeons

21
00:01:50,373 --> 00:01:52,421
here at the Family Heart Center.

22
00:01:52,500 --> 00:01:54,628
We feature the complete Jarvik line,

23
00:01:54,710 --> 00:01:58,181
series 7 Sports Heart by Jensen,
Yamaha.

24
00:01:58,257 --> 00:01:59,930
You pick the heart.

25
00:02:00,008 --> 00:02:02,261
Extended warranties, financing.

26
00:02:02,553 --> 00:02:04,180
Qualifies for health tax credit.

27
00:02:06,432 --> 00:02:08,605
And remember, we care.

28
00:02:10,227 --> 00:02:13,322
Three dead police officers,
one critically injured.

29
00:02:13,397 --> 00:02:17,277
Police union leaders blame
Omni Consumer Products, OCP,

30
00:02:17,359 --> 00:02:20,533
the firm which recently entered
into a contract with the city

31
00:02:20,612 --> 00:02:24,037
to fund and run the Detroit
Metropolitan Police Department.

32
00:02:24,116 --> 00:02:26,539
Dick Jones,
Division President, OCP.

33
00:02:26,618 --> 00:02:28,586
Every policeman knows
when he joins the force

34
00:02:28,662 --> 00:02:31,183
that there are certain inherent risks
that come with the territory.

35
00:02:31,207 --> 00:02:32,379
Ask any cop, he'll tell you,

36
00:02:32,459 --> 00:02:35,020
"If you can't stand the heat,
you better stay out of the kitchen."

37
00:02:35,044 --> 00:02:38,799
Although seriously wounded,
Officer Frank Frederickson escaped

38
00:02:38,882 --> 00:02:40,850
and identified this man.

39
00:02:41,050 --> 00:02:44,680
Clarence Boddicker,
unofficial crime boss of Old Detroit.

40
00:02:44,762 --> 00:02:48,232
Now sought in connection with the
deaths of 31 police officers.

41
00:02:48,516 --> 00:02:49,608
Today, he's at large,

42
00:02:49,684 --> 00:02:52,278
while doctors at
Henry Ford Memorial Hospital

43
00:02:52,353 --> 00:02:55,482
fight to save the life
of Officer Frank Frederickson.

44
00:02:55,565 --> 00:02:56,737
Good luck, Frank.

45
00:03:06,160 --> 00:03:09,664
Attempted murder?
It's not like he killed someone.

46
00:03:09,747 --> 00:03:12,091
This is a clear violation
of my client's civil rights.

47
00:03:12,166 --> 00:03:16,012
Make it aggravated assault,
and I can make bail, in cash, now.

48
00:03:16,086 --> 00:03:19,841
Listen, pal, your client's a scumbag,
you're a scumbag,

49
00:03:19,924 --> 00:03:22,052
and scumbags see the judge
on Monday morning!

50
00:03:22,134 --> 00:03:26,105
Now get out of my police station,
and take laughing boy with you!

51
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:27,477
Get over there!

52
00:03:28,682 --> 00:03:30,962
You have the right to remain
silent. Do you understand me?

53
00:03:31,018 --> 00:03:32,110
Sure, sure.

54
00:03:32,186 --> 00:03:33,904
- Priors?
- No.

55
00:03:33,979 --> 00:03:35,071
Hi.

56
00:03:35,147 --> 00:03:39,028
Uh, Murphy. Transferring in
from Metro South.

57
00:03:39,110 --> 00:03:40,612
Nice precinct.

58
00:03:41,321 --> 00:03:42,698
Yeah, pretty good.

59
00:03:43,657 --> 00:03:47,252
We work for a living down here, Murphy.
Get your armor and suit up.

60
00:03:52,165 --> 00:03:53,883
Please take me home!

61
00:03:53,959 --> 00:03:55,711
Not now, E.J.
Get a cup of coffee.

62
00:03:55,794 --> 00:03:56,886
Oh, Sarge.

63
00:03:56,962 --> 00:03:58,930
Stark, is there any
word on Frederickson?

64
00:03:59,005 --> 00:04:00,723
They're still listing
him as critical.

65
00:04:00,799 --> 00:04:03,143
His wife must be going
out of her mind.

66
00:04:03,218 --> 00:04:04,811
- Murphy, huh?
- Yeah, that's me.

67
00:04:04,886 --> 00:04:06,058
- Manson.
- Hi.

68
00:04:06,137 --> 00:04:07,889
What brings you to
this little paradise?

69
00:04:07,973 --> 00:04:10,648
Beats me, man. I think OCP's moving
a lot of new guys up here.

70
00:04:10,726 --> 00:04:14,651
Omni Consumer Products.
What a bunch of morons.

71
00:04:15,648 --> 00:04:19,448
They're gonna manage this department
right into the ground!

72
00:04:19,860 --> 00:04:21,578
- Where are you from?
- Metro South.

73
00:04:21,654 --> 00:04:22,746
Welcome to hell.

74
00:04:22,822 --> 00:04:24,165
- Murphy.
- Yo.

75
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:26,163
You cut 10 guys
loose over on the east side.

76
00:04:26,242 --> 00:04:28,791
You try to get backup
when you're in a jam.

77
00:04:28,869 --> 00:04:31,588
Yeah, try to get a medevac
after you've been jammed.

78
00:04:31,664 --> 00:04:34,588
I'll tell you what we should do.
We should strike. Fuck 'em!

79
00:04:47,014 --> 00:04:48,186
Oh, boy.

80
00:04:48,640 --> 00:04:49,892
The funeral's tomorrow.

81
00:04:51,518 --> 00:04:55,648
The department requests
all officers not on duty to attend.

82
00:04:56,023 --> 00:05:00,119
Any donations for the family
may be given to Cecil as usual.

83
00:05:03,405 --> 00:05:06,079
And I don't want to hear
any more talk about strike!

84
00:05:06,617 --> 00:05:09,837
We're not plumbers.
We're police officers.

85
00:05:10,787 --> 00:05:12,881
And police officers don't strike.

86
00:05:16,919 --> 00:05:18,921
Murphy, front and center.

87
00:05:37,231 --> 00:05:38,699
Hello, tiger.

88
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:48,997
Hey, hey, hey!

89
00:05:52,247 --> 00:05:53,294
Oh, yes!

90
00:05:55,584 --> 00:05:58,929
Lewis, come here when you're finished
fucking around with your suspect.

91
00:05:59,004 --> 00:06:00,381
Get on your feet!

92
00:06:05,260 --> 00:06:07,638
This guy's gonna be
your new partner.

93
00:06:07,721 --> 00:06:10,224
Murphy, meet Lewis.
Show him the neighborhood.

94
00:06:10,432 --> 00:06:12,275
Glad to know you, Murphy.

95
00:06:12,851 --> 00:06:14,023
Pretty neat.

96
00:06:16,605 --> 00:06:19,609
I better drive until you
know your way around.

97
00:06:20,776 --> 00:06:24,077
I usually drive when I'm
breaking in a new partner.

98
00:06:44,676 --> 00:06:47,555
You really think
the old man is gonna be there?

99
00:06:47,637 --> 00:06:49,230
Why would they invite us?

100
00:06:49,305 --> 00:06:52,104
All division heads are
bringing their support teams.

101
00:06:52,183 --> 00:06:53,526
It's big.

102
00:06:53,601 --> 00:06:55,569
I figure they're green-lighting
Delta City.

103
00:06:55,645 --> 00:06:58,650
What, are you kidding?
They never do anything ahead of schedule.

104
00:06:58,733 --> 00:07:02,283
It's Jones. He's got the 209 series
online and now he wants to show off.

105
00:07:02,361 --> 00:07:04,204
That's a tough break, Bob.

106
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:05,907
What? What?

107
00:07:05,990 --> 00:07:09,494
Well, ED 209 ran into serious
delays and cost overruns.

108
00:07:09,577 --> 00:07:11,671
The old man ordered a backup plan.

109
00:07:11,746 --> 00:07:13,623
95th floor.
Have a nice day.

110
00:07:13,706 --> 00:07:16,084
Probably just to
light a fire under Jones' ass.

111
00:07:16,167 --> 00:07:18,636
- Yeah?
- Old Bob here gets the assignment.

112
00:07:18,711 --> 00:07:19,837
Yeah.

113
00:07:20,129 --> 00:07:23,053
Nobody in Security Concepts
takes it seriously.

114
00:07:23,174 --> 00:07:26,428
It's a better plan. Fucking Jones! I'd
go straight to the Old Man if I could.

115
00:07:26,510 --> 00:07:28,763
Don't mess with Jones, man.
He'll make sushi out of you.

116
00:07:28,846 --> 00:07:31,896
Yeah, you better be careful, man.
I heard Jones is a real shark.

117
00:07:31,975 --> 00:07:33,693
- Who asked you, twerp?
- Bob.

118
00:07:33,769 --> 00:07:35,817
What about this police thing,
what's the problem?

119
00:07:35,896 --> 00:07:37,944
Their union's been bitching
ever since we took over.

120
00:07:38,023 --> 00:07:40,071
You know, the usual nonsense.

121
00:07:40,150 --> 00:07:41,276
We'll turn things around.

122
00:07:41,359 --> 00:07:44,659
Mmm-hmm. Good, very good.
Let's get started.

123
00:07:51,620 --> 00:07:53,122
Now, friends,

124
00:07:54,456 --> 00:07:58,552
I've had this dream
for more than a decade now.

125
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:03,220
A dream which I've invited you all
to share with me.

126
00:08:04,675 --> 00:08:09,602
In six months, we begin construction
of Delta City.

127
00:08:11,349 --> 00:08:13,568
Where Old Detroit now stands.

128
00:08:17,230 --> 00:08:19,232
Old Detroit has a cancer.

129
00:08:20,149 --> 00:08:21,901
The cancer is crime.

130
00:08:22,360 --> 00:08:24,988
And it must be cut out before
we employ the 2 million workers

131
00:08:25,071 --> 00:08:27,165
that will breathe life
into this city again.

132
00:08:27,240 --> 00:08:28,332
Yes.

133
00:08:32,745 --> 00:08:34,793
Although shifts in the tax structure

134
00:08:34,872 --> 00:08:38,127
have created an economy
ideal for corporate growth,

135
00:08:38,252 --> 00:08:41,426
community services,
in this case law enforcement,

136
00:08:42,047 --> 00:08:43,549
have suffered.

137
00:08:44,758 --> 00:08:48,513
I think it's time we
gave something back.

138
00:08:50,430 --> 00:08:51,556
Dick.

139
00:09:02,526 --> 00:09:04,870
Take a close look
at the track record of this company.

140
00:09:06,446 --> 00:09:08,949
And you'll see that we have gambled
in markets

141
00:09:09,032 --> 00:09:11,582
traditionally regarded as nonprofit.

142
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:16,341
Hospitals, prisons,
space exploration.

143
00:09:17,250 --> 00:09:20,129
I say good business
is where you find it.

144
00:09:22,755 --> 00:09:25,099
As you know, we've entered
into a contract with the city

145
00:09:25,174 --> 00:09:27,393
to run local law enforcement.

146
00:09:28,928 --> 00:09:30,726
But at Security Concepts,

147
00:09:30,805 --> 00:09:34,855
we believe an efficient police force
is only part of the solution.

148
00:09:35,268 --> 00:09:37,817
No. We need something more.

149
00:09:38,479 --> 00:09:41,198
We need a 24-hour-a-day
police officer.

150
00:09:41,691 --> 00:09:44,445
A cop that doesn't
need to eat or sleep.

151
00:09:44,987 --> 00:09:48,992
A cop with superior firepower
and the reflexes to use it.

152
00:09:51,076 --> 00:09:52,919
Fellow executives,

153
00:09:52,995 --> 00:09:57,671
it gives me great pleasure to introduce
you to the future of law enforcement.

154
00:10:01,211 --> 00:10:02,588
Ed 209.

155
00:10:39,709 --> 00:10:44,510
The Enforcement Droid series 209 is a
self-sufficient law enforcement robot.

156
00:10:45,215 --> 00:10:47,809
209 is currently programmed
for urban pacification,

157
00:10:47,884 --> 00:10:49,636
but that is only the beginning.

158
00:10:50,096 --> 00:10:52,815
After a successful tour of duty
in Old Detroit,

159
00:10:52,890 --> 00:10:57,691
we can expect 209 to become the hot
military product for the next decade.

160
00:10:58,896 --> 00:11:00,990
- Dr. McNamara.
- We'll need an arrest subject.

161
00:11:01,065 --> 00:11:02,317
- Mr. Kinney.
- Yes, sir?

162
00:11:02,400 --> 00:11:03,669
Would you come up
and give us a hand, please?

163
00:11:03,693 --> 00:11:04,990
Yes, sir.

164
00:11:05,069 --> 00:11:09,916
Mr. Kinney is going to help us simulate
a typical arrest and disarming procedure.

165
00:11:10,074 --> 00:11:13,248
Mr. Kinney, use your gun
in a threatening manner.

166
00:11:15,329 --> 00:11:17,582
- Point it at Ed 209.
- Yes, sir.

167
00:11:26,508 --> 00:11:30,934
Please put down your weapon.
You have 20 seconds to comply.

168
00:11:32,431 --> 00:11:35,605
I think you'd better do what he says,
Mr. Kinney.

169
00:11:40,480 --> 00:11:43,780
You now have 15 seconds to comply.

170
00:11:43,942 --> 00:11:46,087
- You are in direct violation...
- Cut the power! Pull the board!

171
00:11:46,111 --> 00:11:49,536
Of Penal Code 113, Section 9.

172
00:11:49,614 --> 00:11:51,054
You now have five seconds to comply.

173
00:11:52,117 --> 00:11:53,209
Help! Help me!

174
00:11:53,285 --> 00:11:55,879
Four, three, two, one.

175
00:11:57,415 --> 00:12:00,385
I am now authorized to
use physical force.

176
00:12:25,151 --> 00:12:26,323
It's horrible.

177
00:12:26,402 --> 00:12:28,496
Somebody want to call
a goddamn paramedic?

178
00:12:28,571 --> 00:12:31,826
- Let's go, Johnson!
- You pull the plug on this thing!

179
00:12:33,118 --> 00:12:35,166
All right, don't touch him.

180
00:12:35,621 --> 00:12:37,089
Don't touch him!

181
00:12:37,164 --> 00:12:38,336
He didn't hear the gun drop.

182
00:12:38,415 --> 00:12:39,758
He didn't hear it?

183
00:12:40,834 --> 00:12:42,086
Oh, God.

184
00:12:42,169 --> 00:12:44,797
Dick, I'm very disappointed.

185
00:12:46,465 --> 00:12:49,344
I'm sure it's only a glitch,
a temporary setback.

186
00:12:49,426 --> 00:12:51,349
You call this a glitch?

187
00:12:53,138 --> 00:12:55,436
We're scheduled to begin construction
in six months.

188
00:12:55,516 --> 00:12:59,441
Your temporary setback could cost us $50
million in interest payments alone.

189
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:01,238
Not necessarily, sir.

190
00:13:01,313 --> 00:13:03,111
Perhaps you're aware
of the Robocop program

191
00:13:03,190 --> 00:13:04,943
developed by myself
at Security Concepts

192
00:13:05,026 --> 00:13:07,120
as a contingency
against just this sort of thing.

193
00:13:07,195 --> 00:13:08,742
Thank you for your concern,
Mr. Morton.

194
00:13:08,822 --> 00:13:10,841
I'm sure this is something
we can take up in my office...

195
00:13:10,865 --> 00:13:11,866
Now, wait a minute. Dick!

196
00:13:12,033 --> 00:13:13,751
Get me out of here!

197
00:13:14,828 --> 00:13:17,923
Maybe what we need here
is a fresh perspective.

198
00:13:18,248 --> 00:13:21,127
Tell me about your plan, Mr. Morton.
How long will it take?

199
00:13:21,209 --> 00:13:22,210
We're ready to go, sir.

200
00:13:22,293 --> 00:13:23,966
We've restructured the
police department

201
00:13:24,045 --> 00:13:26,139
and placed prime candidates
according to risk factor.

202
00:13:26,214 --> 00:13:28,637
I'm confident that we can go
to prototype within 90 days.

203
00:13:28,716 --> 00:13:31,344
Good, very good.
Get your staff together, Mr. Morton.

204
00:13:31,427 --> 00:13:34,055
I'll expect a full presentation
in 20 minutes.

205
00:13:34,722 --> 00:13:36,224
Thank you, sir.

206
00:13:42,565 --> 00:13:44,793
Yes! Now, that's how it's done
in the big leagues, Johnson.

207
00:13:44,817 --> 00:13:47,286
You see an opening, you go for it.

208
00:13:48,112 --> 00:13:51,582
You better watch your back, Bob.
Jones is going to come looking for you.

209
00:13:51,699 --> 00:13:55,579
Fuck Jones. He fumbled the ball
and I was there to pick it up.

210
00:13:56,245 --> 00:13:58,088
Too bad about Kinney.

211
00:13:58,330 --> 00:14:00,458
That's life in the big city.

212
00:14:01,500 --> 00:14:03,093
When do we start?

213
00:14:03,169 --> 00:14:05,888
As soon as
some poor schmuck volunteers.

214
00:14:06,630 --> 00:14:08,883
Unit 3509, proceed to Hall and Grand.

215
00:14:08,966 --> 00:14:10,844
411 involving indigents.

216
00:14:10,927 --> 00:14:13,271
Roger, we're on our way.

217
00:14:22,898 --> 00:14:25,117
Pretty fancy moves, Murphy.

218
00:14:25,192 --> 00:14:28,617
Yeah, my son, Jimmy,
watches this cop show, TJ Lazer,

219
00:14:28,695 --> 00:14:31,665
and this Lazer guy does this
every time he takes down a bad guy.

220
00:14:31,740 --> 00:14:34,118
So naturally, my kid thinks
every good cop should be...

221
00:14:34,201 --> 00:14:36,124
And you don't want to disappoint him.

222
00:14:36,912 --> 00:14:40,837
Yeah, well, role models
can be very important to a boy.

223
00:14:47,590 --> 00:14:49,718
Okay, okay, I get a kick out of it.

224
00:14:49,800 --> 00:14:51,894
All units,
all units, sector 9.

225
00:14:51,969 --> 00:14:53,812
- That's for...
- 211 in progress.

226
00:14:54,305 --> 00:14:55,978
Why don't you drive?

227
00:14:56,641 --> 00:14:59,895
The suspects are armed
and considered dangerous.

228
00:15:02,480 --> 00:15:03,697
CLARENCE; Shit.

229
00:15:05,066 --> 00:15:06,613
I don't believe it!

230
00:15:06,692 --> 00:15:07,784
What?

231
00:15:07,860 --> 00:15:10,079
You burned the fucking money!

232
00:15:10,154 --> 00:15:12,202
I had to blow the door.
What do you want?

233
00:15:12,281 --> 00:15:14,283
It's as good as marked, you asshole!

234
00:15:14,367 --> 00:15:16,746
You stupid, stupid asshole!

235
00:15:16,828 --> 00:15:19,422
- Clarence!
- What? What do you want?

236
00:15:19,498 --> 00:15:21,171
We got a cop on our tail.

237
00:15:28,423 --> 00:15:30,266
Come on, man, speed it up! Move it!

238
00:15:30,342 --> 00:15:32,515
This crate ain't gonna outrun a cop.

239
00:15:32,594 --> 00:15:35,188
- Slow down, then.
- What, are you crazy, man?

240
00:15:35,264 --> 00:15:38,188
Shut the fuck up and do it!
Just do it!

241
00:15:38,267 --> 00:15:41,146
Central, this is 154.
We're in pursuit of 211 suspect.

242
00:15:41,228 --> 00:15:42,400
Request backup.

243
00:15:42,771 --> 00:15:44,364
Roger, 154.

244
00:15:44,439 --> 00:15:47,033
- Backup currently unavailable.
- Give me your piece.

245
00:15:47,484 --> 00:15:49,612
Backup E.T.A., 15 minutes.

246
00:15:49,861 --> 00:15:51,284
Bobby, get the door!

247
00:15:51,531 --> 00:15:52,623
Everybody load up!

248
